    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0795" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2100</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-07T21:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1915, 9 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 8, 11 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2854. I have had no news from you about submarine negotiations, notes, or
                    position. Von Jagow complained to-day that he had no news whatever from
                    Bernstorff; that as you have German cipher, communication of confidential nature
                    by wireless is useless and that you refuse to transmit cipher to Bernstorff
                    through me. Hope you will at least let me know what has happened and authorize
                    me to inform Von Jagow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
